---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Give a comment thread a color, or move it to a point or onto an object; one of --color, --at and --object is needed.
It prints the thread and what changed.

USAGE
  holst comment edit <board> <thread> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board    The board
  thread   The thread: its thread id, e.g. weVza, or @N from `holst comment ls`

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws    Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --color color     The color of the thread, or none to clear it
      --at x,y          Move the thread to this corner in board units; not with --object
      --object object   Move the thread onto this object: id, link or the first 8 characters of its id; not with --at
  -n, --dry-run         Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst comment edit "Roadmap" weVza --color red10
  $ holst comment edit "Roadmap" weVza --at 120,80
  $ holst comment edit "Roadmap" @2 --object a1b2c3d4 --color none

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
